<title>Video.save Function</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
b = video_name.save(<arg>video_file_path</arg>);
</logicsyntax>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <logiccolor>Video.save</logiccolor> function writes the contents of the <link Video.csdoc>Video</link> object to a file specified by the string expression <arg>video_file_path</arg>.

Video recorded using the function <logiccolor>Video.recordInteractive</logiccolor> is stored in <link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebM">WebM</link> format and should be saved with the extension .webm so that it will be recognized by media players.


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

The function returns a logical value of <logiccolor>1</logiccolor> (<logiccolor>true</logiccolor>) if the video was saved, <logiccolor>0</logiccolor> (<logiccolor>false</logiccolor>) if there was an error writing the file, and <logiccolor>default</logiccolor> if the Video object does not contain a video recording.


